      "title": "Metal levels",
      "narration": "Every marketplace plan covers the same essential health benefits; the metal level tells you how the cost is split. Actuarial value is the share of covered costs the plan pays for a standard population. Bronze plans pay about 60 percent, silver about 70, gold about 80 and platinum about 90. Lower metals mean lower premiums and higher deductibles. Catastrophic plans, with very high deductibles, are limited to people under 30 or those with a hardship exemption. Marcus’s daughter, turning 26 and healthy, might pick bronze; Rosa, who expects a surgery, might pick gold.",
