      "title": "The small business marketplace",
      "narration": "Maryland Health Connection runs the state’s individual Exchange and a Small Business Health Options Program, or SHOP, for employers with up to 50 employees. In SHOP the employer picks a contribution level and one or more plans, employees enroll, and the employer receives a single consolidated bill and pays it; the marketplace or its administrator distributes premiums to the carriers. Enrollment may run through an authorized producer. Employers with fewer than 25 full-time equivalent employees and modest average wages may qualify for the small business health care tax credit, available only for coverage bought through SHOP, for two consecutive years.",
