      "title": "Internal appeal",
      "narration": "When a plan denies a claim, refuses to authorize care or rescinds coverage, that is an adverse benefit determination, and the member may appeal. The first step is an internal appeal to the plan, requested within 180 days of the denial. The plan must have the appeal reviewed by someone not involved in the original decision and, for medical judgments, by an appropriate clinician. Decisions are due within 30 days for care not yet received and 60 days for care already received. Urgent cases get an expedited decision; Maryland requires emergency grievance decisions within 24 hours. The member may see the file and submit evidence.",
