      "title": "External review",
      "narration": "If the plan upholds a denial based on medical necessity or similar judgment, the member may seek external review by an independent party. In Maryland, the Insurance Administration handles complaints about adverse decisions, obtains an independent medical review when needed, and its determination binds the carrier. The Attorney General’s Health Education and Advocacy Unit helps consumers file grievances and gather records. External review is free to the member and must be decided within set time limits, with expedited review for urgent care. A member may also skip the internal step when the carrier fails to follow its own process or the case is urgent.",
