      "title": "Subsidies",
      "narration": "People who buy through the individual Exchange may qualify for a premium tax credit based on household income relative to the federal poverty level. The credit is usually paid in advance directly to the insurer, lowering the monthly premium, and is reconciled on the tax return. It is not available to people offered affordable employer coverage or eligible for Medicaid; in Maryland, adults with income below 138 percent of poverty generally qualify for Medicaid instead. Cost-sharing reductions lower deductibles and copayments for enrollees between 100 and 250 percent of poverty, but only in silver plans. The income ranges and credit amounts are set by Congress and change, so check current figures.",
